1
00:00:00,190 --> 00:00:05,544
Two weeks ago, the rule was simple:
never boil your broccoli, because

2
00:00:05,544 --> 00:00:10,510
heat destroys the enzyme that
makes its most important molecule.

3
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:16,110
Today, I am going to tell
you to cook your tomatoes.

4
00:00:16,830 --> 00:00:20,239
And the reason those two
statements do not contradict

5
00:00:20,239 --> 00:00:23,070
each other is the whole
point of this video.

6
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:27,150
A raw tomato is not the
best version of a tomato.

7
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:28,750
Cooking it

8
00:00:28,830 --> 00:00:34,677
The thing everyone tells you destroys
nutrients, makes its most valuable

9
00:00:34,677 --> 00:00:39,550
molecule several times easier
for your body to actually use.

10
00:00:40,270 --> 00:00:43,950
The red in a tomato is a
pigment called lycopene.

11
00:00:44,510 --> 00:00:49,230
It belongs to the same family as the
beta carotene that makes carrots orange.

12
00:00:49,870 --> 00:00:53,470
But inside a raw tomato,
lycopene is not free.

13
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:57,869
It sits inside structures
called chromoplasts,

14
00:00:57,869 --> 00:01:01,350
bound into a matrix of
protein and membrane.

15
00:01:02,390 --> 00:01:05,190
Your digestion is not good
at breaking that open.

16
00:01:05,830 --> 00:01:10,075
Eat a raw tomato, and much of
the lycopene passes through you

17
00:01:10,075 --> 00:01:14,390
still locked inside the fragments
of plant cell it arrived in.

18
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:17,910
Heat does three things to that.

19
00:01:18,630 --> 00:01:21,830
First, it ruptures the cell walls.

20
00:01:22,470 --> 00:01:24,270
Mechanical release.

21
00:01:24,470 --> 00:01:29,510
The pigment is no longer trapped behind
cellulose your enzymes cannot cut.

22
00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:34,947
Second, it denatures the proteins
holding the pigment in place, so

23
00:01:34,947 --> 00:01:39,750
the molecule comes free rather
than staying bound to a structure.

24
00:01:40,630 --> 00:01:43,446
Third, and this is the
interesting one, heat

25
00:01:43,446 --> 00:01:46,070
changes the shape of the molecule itself.

26
00:01:47,270 --> 00:01:51,427
In a raw tomato, most
lycopene is a straight,

27
00:01:51,427 --> 00:01:55,030
rod-like form, called the trans isomer.

28
00:01:55,910 --> 00:02:02,191
Heat bends it into cis isomers, and that
bent shape packs far more easily into

29
00:02:02,191 --> 00:02:08,150
the micelles that carry fat-soluble
molecules across your intestinal wall.

30
00:02:09,350 --> 00:02:11,510
Straight molecules stack badly.

31
00:02:12,310 --> 00:02:14,110
Bent ones fit.

32
00:02:14,350 --> 00:02:17,818
So the same amount of
lycopene, cooked, reaches

33
00:02:17,818 --> 00:02:20,990
your bloodstream in
much larger quantities.

34
00:02:21,710 --> 00:02:27,420
In controlled human studies, lycopene
from tomato paste was absorbed several

35
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:32,830
times better than lycopene from an
equivalent portion of fresh tomatoes.

36
00:02:33,550 --> 00:02:35,350
There is a second multiplier.

37
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:41,710
Lycopene is fat-soluble, so without fat,
there are no micelles waiting for it.

38
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:45,830
Cooking tomatoes in olive
oil is not just flavour.

39
00:02:46,390 --> 00:02:48,310
It completes the delivery system.

40
00:02:48,950 --> 00:02:51,430
Same mechanism we covered with avocado.

41
00:02:51,990 --> 00:02:53,790
The fat is not the nutrient.

42
00:02:54,070 --> 00:02:55,830
The fat is the vehicle.

43
00:02:55,910 --> 00:02:57,710
Now follow it past the intestine.

44
00:02:58,630 --> 00:03:02,911
Absorbed lycopene is packed
into chylomicrons, enters

45
00:03:02,911 --> 00:03:07,030
the lymphatic system, and
reaches your bloodstream.

46
00:03:07,750 --> 00:03:11,350
From there, it transfers
into your lipoproteins.

47
00:03:11,750 --> 00:03:13,550
And this is where it gets specific.

48
00:03:14,470 --> 00:03:18,710
Lycopene concentrates
inside LDL particles.

49
00:03:19,510 --> 00:03:20,870
That matters.

50
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:25,670
Because the first step in
arterial plaque is not LDL itself.

51
00:03:26,950 --> 00:03:31,830
It is LDL becoming oxidised
inside the artery wall.

52
00:03:32,470 --> 00:03:36,505
An oxidised LDL particle
is what a macrophage

53
00:03:36,505 --> 00:03:40,630
swallows uncontrollably
to become a foam cell.

54
00:03:41,310 --> 00:03:46,670
Lycopene riding inside that particle
sits exactly where the damage starts.

55
00:03:47,230 --> 00:03:49,390
It also builds up in tissue.

56
00:03:50,270 --> 00:03:54,546
The liver, the adrenal glands,
the testes and the prostate

57
00:03:54,546 --> 00:03:57,790
hold the highest
concentrations in the body.

58
00:03:58,830 --> 00:04:00,750
So what does the evidence say?

59
00:04:01,790 --> 00:04:03,950
Here it splits, and I want to be careful.

60
00:04:05,310 --> 00:04:08,510
On observational data, it is consistent.

61
00:04:09,950 --> 00:04:13,908
People with higher lycopene
intake, and more importantly

62
00:04:13,908 --> 00:04:17,936
higher lycopene measured in
their blood, show lower rates

63
00:04:17,936 --> 00:04:21,470
of cardiovascular disease
across many populations.

64
00:04:22,270 --> 00:04:24,590
Meta-analyses of those studies agree.

65
00:04:25,310 --> 00:04:27,630
On randomised trials, it is thinner.

66
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:33,514
Supplementing isolated lycopene
has not reliably reproduced

67
00:04:33,514 --> 00:04:36,590
the benefit seen in
people who eat tomatoes.

68
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:39,910
That gap usually means one of two things.

69
00:04:40,390 --> 00:04:44,108
Either the whole food matters
more than the single molecule,

70
00:04:44,108 --> 00:04:46,710
or the association was never fully causal.

71
00:04:47,350 --> 00:04:49,510
We do not yet know which.

72
00:04:50,710 --> 00:04:54,310
On prostate cancer, be sceptical
of what you have heard.

73
00:04:54,870 --> 00:04:58,079
The claim was strong in the
nineteen nineties, and has

74
00:04:58,079 --> 00:05:01,110
been steadily downgraded
as better studies arrived.

75
00:05:01,590 --> 00:05:04,270
Regulators now describe that
evidence as very limited.

76
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:07,150
Mechanism.

77
00:05:07,230 --> 00:05:08,990
Strong.

78
00:05:09,070 --> 00:05:11,390
Population data, consistent.

79
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:15,150
Isolated supplement trials, disappointing.

80
00:05:15,870 --> 00:05:17,630
So, four rules.

81
00:05:17,710 --> 00:05:18,830
One.

82
00:05:18,910 --> 00:05:20,190
Cook them.

83
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:24,030
Sauce, roasted, stewed, or paste.

84
00:05:24,910 --> 00:05:28,379
The processed form is genuinely
the better source here,

85
00:05:28,379 --> 00:05:31,470
which is rare enough to
be worth saying out loud.

86
00:05:32,830 --> 00:05:33,950
Two.

87
00:05:34,030 --> 00:05:35,830
Cook them in oil.

88
00:05:36,030 --> 00:05:38,830
Without fat, the lycopene
has no way across.

89
00:05:40,030 --> 00:05:41,310
Three.

90
00:05:41,390 --> 00:05:46,270
Tomato paste is the most concentrated
lycopene source in an ordinary kitchen.

91
00:05:46,990 --> 00:05:50,990
One spoonful carries more
than several fresh tomatoes.

92
00:05:51,950 --> 00:05:53,310
Four.

93
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:57,710
Keep some raw, because cooking
does cost you vitamin C.

94
00:05:58,270 --> 00:06:00,590
This is a real trade, not a free upgrade.

95
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:06,070
Cooked for lycopene, raw
for vitamin C, and eat both.

96
00:06:06,790 --> 00:06:08,150
Two quick notes.

97
00:06:08,230 --> 00:06:13,110
Very high long-term intake can
tint the skin faintly orange.

98
00:06:13,590 --> 00:06:15,830
It is harmless, and it reverses.

99
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:20,259
And if you have reflux, tomato
is a common trigger, which has

100
00:06:20,259 --> 00:06:24,070
nothing to do with lycopene and
everything to do with acidity.

101
00:06:24,830 --> 00:06:26,910
None of this was really about a tomato.

102
00:06:27,310 --> 00:06:32,415
It was about a molecule that is
present but unavailable, and the fact

103
00:06:32,415 --> 00:06:37,150
that how you prepare your food
decides which of those two it is.

104
00:06:38,270 --> 00:06:40,070
So which molecule should we follow next?

105
00:06:41,390 --> 00:06:44,340
Write a food and an organ in the comments,

106
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:47,150
and we will take it apart, cell by cell.
